INT. COURTHOUSE BASEMENT, EXHIBIT STORAGE - DAY

Fluorescent tubes. Metal shelving. Cardboard boxes labeled in marker.

Three people stand at a steel table, a single evidence bag between them.

ATTORNEY SABINE OKONKWO-HARTLEY (40s, gray suit, tired) holds a tablet.

OPPOSING COUNSEL DOMINIC TRAVERSO-ADEBAYO (50s, expensive tie, patient smile) flips through an inventory.

CLERK PRUDENCE "PRU" LINDGREN-ASANTE (20s, lanyard, headphones around her neck) logs entries on a clipboard.

SABINE
(to the room)
For the record, we are inspecting Exhibit Fourteen.

DOMINIC
For the record, it's a screwdriver.

PRU
It's a Phillips-head.

SABINE
Thank you, Pru.

DOMINIC
Sabine, we've been through this.

SABINE
Dominic, we've been through everything.

DOMINIC
The chain of custody is solid.

SABINE
The chain of custody has a gap of nineteen hours.

DOMINIC
That was a weekend.

SABINE
Murder trials don't have weekends.

DOMINIC
This one did.

PRU
(muttering)
I'm just the clerk.

SABINE
Pru, which officer logged the tool?

PRU
Officer Haverford. Badge four-two-one.

DOMINIC
He's on leave.

SABINE
Convenient.

DOMINIC
Medical.

SABINE
Of course.

PRU
(to herself)
Of course.

Sabine leans over the bag. Squints at a smudge on the handle.

SABINE
That's a thumbprint.

DOMINIC
Probably the officer's.

SABINE
Probably.

DOMINIC
Is there a point?

SABINE
There's a name in the margin of the log. Not Haverford.

Pru checks her clipboard. Her eyes widen.

PRU
Oh.

DOMINIC
Pru?

PRU
It says... Traverso.

Dominic's smile doesn't move.

SABINE
Your father's name.

DOMINIC
(evenly)
It's a common name.

SABINE
It's a very uncommon screwdriver.

Pru backs a step toward the stairs. Sabine, calm, unfolds her tablet.

SABINE (CONT'D)
(to the ceiling)
Let the record show opposing counsel declined to comment.

DOMINIC
(to himself)
Neither confirmed nor denied.

SABINE
(overlapping)
That's the same thing.

DOMINIC
(overlapping)
It is not.

^

Pru, very softly, closes the log.
